[patterns/application/extensions/PTN-APP-EXT-010-rule-engine-extension-pattern.md#pattern-description]

### Pattern Description

This pattern provides multiple approaches for rule-based extensions:

**Approach 1: Embedded Rule Engine (RulesEngine or CoreRulesEngine)**

Embed .NET rule engine directly in extension:

```csharp
public class TexasClaimsRulesExtension : IClaimValidator
{
    private readonly RulesEngine _rulesEngine;

    public TexasClaimsRulesExtension()
    {
        // Load rules from JSON
        var rulesJson = LoadRulesConfiguration();
        _rulesEngine = new RulesEngine(rulesJson, null);
    }

    public async Task<ValidationResult> ValidateAsync(Claim claim, CancellationToken ct)
    {
        var ruleInput = new RuleParameter("claim", claim);
        var results = await _rulesEngine.ExecuteAllRulesAsync("TexasClaimValidation", ruleInput);

        var errors = results
            .Where(r => !r.IsSuccess)
            .Select(r => r.ExceptionMessage)
            .ToList();

        return errors.Any()
            ? ValidationResult.Invalid(errors)
            : ValidationResult.Valid();
    }
}
```

**Rule Definition (JSON)**:

```json
{
  "WorkflowName": "TexasClaimValidation",
  "Rules": [
    {
      "RuleName": "HighValueClaimCheck",
      "ErrorMessage": "Claims over $10,000 require prior authorization",
      "ErrorType": "Warning",
      "RuleExpressionType": "LambdaExpression",
      "Expression": "claim.Amount > 10000 AND claim.PriorAuthNumber == null"
    },
    {
      "RuleName": "ProviderEnrollmentCheck",
      "ErrorMessage": "Provider is not enrolled in Texas Medicaid",
      "ErrorType": "Error",
      "Expression": "claim.Provider.EnrolledStates.Contains(\"Texas\") == false"
    },
    {
      "RuleName": "ServiceDateValidation",
      "ErrorMessage": "Service date cannot be more than 365 days old",
      "ErrorType": "Error",
      "Expression": "(DateTime.Today - claim.ServiceDate).TotalDays > 365"
    }
  ]
}
```

**Approach 2: DSL-Based Rules**

Create domain-specific language for rule authoring:

```csharp
// Texas eligibility rules in custom DSL
RULE "Texas_Adult_Eligibility"
  WHEN
    Applicant.Age >= 19 AND
    Applicant.Age <= 64 AND
    Applicant.Income <= FederalPovertyLevel * 1.33 AND
    Applicant.ResidencyMonths >= 6
  THEN
    Approve(Category: "Adults")
ENDRULE

RULE "Texas_Child_Eligibility"
  WHEN
    Applicant.Age < 19 AND
    Applicant.Income <= FederalPovertyLevel * 2.00
  THEN
    Approve(Category: "CHIP")
ENDRULE
```

**Approach 3: Rule Composition**

Compose complex rules from simpler building blocks:

```csharp
public class FloridaClaimRules
{
    private readonly IRule<Claim> _providerEnrollment;
    private readonly IRule<Claim> _serviceAuthorization;
    private readonly IRule<Claim> _amountLimits;

    public FloridaClaimRules()
    {
        // Individual rules
        _providerEnrollment = new ProviderEnrollmentRule("Florida");
        _serviceAuthorization = new ServiceAuthorizationRule();
        _amountLimits = new AmountLimitRule(maxAmount: 50000);
    }

    public ValidationResult Validate(Claim claim)
    {
        // Compose rules with AND logic
        var compositeRule = _providerEnrollment
            .And(_serviceAuthorization)
            .And(_amountLimits);

        return compositeRule.Evaluate(claim);
    }
}

public interface IRule<T>
{
    ValidationResult Evaluate(T input);
    IRule<T> And(IRule<T> other);
    IRule<T> Or(IRule<T> other);
}
```

**Decision Matrix: Rules vs. Code**

```
Criteria                  | Use Rules | Use Code
--------------------------|-----------|----------
Change frequency          | Weekly    | Monthly+
Stakeholder visibility    | Business  | Developers
Complexity (conditions)   | <15       | 15+
Performance requirement   | <100ms    | Any
Testing approach          | Data-driven| Unit tests
Algorithmic logic         | No        | Yes
Calculations              | Simple    | Complex
Debugging needs           | Low       | High
```

**Integration Pattern**:

```csharp
public class HybridClaimProcessor : IClaimProcessor
{
    private readonly RulesEngine _rulesEngine;
    private readonly IComplexCalculationService _calcService;

    public async Task<ClaimResult> ProcessAsync(Claim claim)
    {
        // Step 1: Rules-based validation (frequently changing business logic)
        var validationResult = await ValidateWithRulesAsync(claim);
        if (!validationResult.IsValid)
            return ClaimResult.Rejected(validationResult.Errors);

        // Step 2: Code-based processing (complex algorithms)
        var adjustedAmount = await _calcService.CalculateAdjustmentsAsync(claim);
        claim.AdjustedAmount = adjustedAmount;

        // Step 3: Rules-based approval determination
        var approvalResult = await EvaluateApprovalRulesAsync(claim);

        return approvalResult.IsApproved
            ? ClaimResult.Approved(claim)
            : ClaimResult.PendingReview(claim, approvalResult.Reason);
    }
}
```

